</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Benchmark construction</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We construct the benchmark in three stages: adapt source tasks, build task
families through two complementary routes, and validate the resulting cases.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Source adaptation.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select tasks with clear requirements and meaningful variation from six
benchmarks: Terminal-Bench and AgentIF-OneDay
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Merrill et al., 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, SpreadsheetBench
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, CodeContests and FullStackBench
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>, and OfficeBench
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. We normalize their formats and align descriptions,
fixtures, and scorers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task-family construction.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experts in coding and agent benchmarking collaborate with agents through two
routes (Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>A): <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">extraction and adaptation</span>
groups compatible source cases under a shared specification and aligns
their statements and tests; <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">seed expansion</span> starts from one task,
defines its invariant goal and permitted variation, and authors additional
cases within that scope. Both routes yield a public family specification
and executable variants. One fixed case serves as the acquisition anchor;
the remaining cases provide candidates for held-out evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Validation.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each case includes a resettable environment, a reference solution, and
private tests. Programmatic checks verify Docker builds, execute tests,
and confirm that reference solutions pass them; an expert other than the
author then reviews each case before acceptance. Reference solutions and
private tests remain outside agent workspaces (Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Benchmark Assets and Evaluation Cohorts ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Catalog and evaluation cohorts.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">full catalog</span> contains 35 families and
408 cases across six domains, with
5–17 cases per family, including the anchor
(Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Catalog and evaluation cohorts. ‣ 3.2 Benchmark construction ‣ 3 SkillTransferBench ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">main cohort</span> selects families
with at least 5 verified held-out cases and at least two
non-perfect outcomes in catalog-wide No-Skill screening, yielding
22 families and 155 held-out cases
(Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.2 Catalog and variation axes ‣ Appendix B Benchmark Assets and Evaluation Cohorts ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>); its <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lite subset</span> covers
10 families and 77 cases across all six domains
for comparisons across model pairs. Each pair independently acquires its
own packages.</p>
</div>
