<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">How do teaching, Student actions, and package revisions change as
Skill acquisition progresses?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> traces 630 reviews across
66 Qwen <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Fixed-Window SSL</span> runs with 3 rounds each,
linking Educator-reported intents, Student actions, and package snapshots. We compare
behavior following teaching and silence at regular reviews, standardizing
by round. Appendices <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Teaching-intervention taxonomy and dialogue turns ‣ Appendix E Teaching Process Analysis ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> and <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Review decisions and subsequent Student behavior ‣ Appendix E Teaching Process Analysis ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> detail the taxonomy
and estimation.</p>
</div>
