<td id="S5.T3.6.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.45pt 3.0pt;"><span id="S5.T3.6.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">210</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The Qwen HTML-finance case shows how Student checks refine teaching advice.
The Educator proposes deriving reported values from other entries to detect
inconsistency. The Student’s initial implementation flags
4 metrics where only one is wrong. After inspecting this
output, the Student replaces generic arithmetic with financial relations
and reverse derivations, isolating the actual error (Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
The final Skill retains these relations and distinguishes an untested value
from a contradicted one. On an unseen cash-flow report, a fresh solver reads
the package, checks accounting relations, and passes
4/4 checks (Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Case Evidence and Frozen-Package Use ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>).
The lesson initiates an investigation; the Student’s execution evidence
determines how the proposal becomes reusable knowledge.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Fixed review intervals become increasingly costly as this need for guidance
declines. Average tokens per review grow 5.3-fold from the
first to the last round as context accumulates; reviews returning silence
account for 85.8% of final-round review tokens,
before follow-up dialogue. This mismatch motivates selecting reviews around
unresolved work while allowing the Student’s investigation to continue.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>RQ4: Selecting and focusing review around unresolved issues</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Can selecting and focusing review around unresolved issues preserve
transfer while reducing expert supervision?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 5.4 RQ4: Selecting and focusing review around unresolved issues ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> compares fixed reviews every <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=5,10,20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=5,10,20</annotation></semantics></math>
Student tool calls with <span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Issue-Guided SSL</span> on the Qwen main cohort, using
3 rounds and 66 runs per schedule.
We prioritize Educator tokens to measure demand for external expertise,
and track how Student work changes total acquisition cost.
Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 RQ2: Organizing expert guidance during Skill acquisition ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(b) extends the comparison to DeepSeek and Kimi
on the shared 10 families. Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="Cost accounting. ‣ C.3 Acquisition comparators ‣ Appendix C Protocols, Implementation, and Reproduction ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>
defines the cost components for each model pair.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S5.F5.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:143.6pt;">
<p id="S5.F5.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.F5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">(a) Utility</span></p><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.17860v1/efficiency_a.svg" id="S5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:199/122;" width="199" height="122"></object>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
