<p id="S5.F5.3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.F5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">(b) Teaching cost</span></p><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.17860v1/efficiency_b.svg" id="S5.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:130/122;" width="130" height="122"></object>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:107.3pt;">
<p id="S5.F5.4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.F5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">(c) Gain per cost</span></p><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.17860v1/efficiency_c.svg" id="S5.F5.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:148/122;" width="148" height="122"></object>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="S5.F5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transfer utility and teaching efficiency across review schedules.</span>
Qwen main cohort: 22 families, 155 cases, 3 repeats.
Panels compare (a) family-macro utility, (b) Educator tokens, and
(c) transfer gain over No Skill per million Educator tokens,
with shared schedule rows.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Issue-guided review reaches 0.805 utility versus 0.801
for the standard <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=10</annotation></semantics></math> window, using 61.7% fewer
Educator tokens and 16.9% fewer acquisition tokens.
It achieves 2.75 times the transfer gain per
Educator token.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Simply changing the interval does not recover this balance:
<math id="S5.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=5</annotation></semantics></math> increases Educator cost, whereas <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=20</annotation></semantics></math> reduces it, but both yield
lower utility. Compared with <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=10</annotation></semantics></math>, Issue-Guided SSL reduces review count
by 47.8% and tokens per review (including follow-up dialogue)
by 26.7%.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">On DeepSeek and Kimi, Issue-Guided SSL uses 63.8%
and 77.4% fewer Educator tokens, respectively, while
retaining utility within one percentage point of Fixed-Window SSL.
Total acquisition tokens also fall for Kimi; additional Student work raises
the total for DeepSeek (Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Review Scheduling and Cost Allocation ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussion and Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On shared <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SkillTransferBench</span> families across three model pairs, Socratic
Skill Learning (<span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SSL</span>) improves transfer over direct expert authoring
and post-hoc teaching. Process and case analyses show how guidance enters
Skill development: advice identifies a direction to investigate, while
execution evidence informs how the Student tests, adapts, and retains a
procedure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As teaching demand changes, unresolved questions provide a basis for
allocating expert attention. Issue-Guided SSL tracks these questions across
revisions, retaining transfer utility with 2.75
times the gain per Educator token of Fixed-Window SSL on the main cohort.
The study connects the development of reusable knowledge with decisions
about where further guidance is needed.</p>
</div>
</section>
