<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Validation and acceptance</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Acceptance requires a stable family invariant with declared variation,
unambiguous requirements with deterministic tests, tasks that go beyond
mechanical edits, and at least three separately attributable checks.
Programmatic validation verifies Docker builds, executes tests, and
confirms that reference solutions pass them. An expert other than the
author reviews each case before acceptance. Reference solutions and
private tests remain outside agent workspaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Curation yields 35 families and 408 cases from
37 candidate families and 444
cases. Reference solutions pass all 2,807 checks
(3–34 per case).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Evaluation cohort</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main cohort selects families with at least 5 verified
held-out cases and at least two non-perfect outcomes in catalog-wide
No-Skill screening. It contains 22 families and
155 held-out cases, with 5–10
cases per family, retaining ceiling cases for coverage and regression
measurement.
Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Repeat variation, non-ceiling cases, and sensitivity ‣ Appendix D Supplementary Transfer Results ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> reports repeat-level scores and case-level
transfer directions.</p>
</div>
