<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Full-pass gains over No Skill are 16.99 percentage points
for <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Fixed-Window SSL</span> (95% paired family-bootstrap CI:
<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[8.13,26.86]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>8.13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26.86</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[8.13,26.86]</annotation></semantics></math>) and 18.33 points for
<span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Issue-Guided SSL</span> (<math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[9.44,28.12]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>9.44</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>28.12</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[9.44,28.12]</annotation></semantics></math>), using the same family resampling
as the utility comparisons.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fixed-Window SSL’s paired gains are 7.29 points over Expert Authoring,
5.31 over Post-hoc Teaching, 3.99 over Trace2Skill,
and 4.99 over adapted SKILL-KD.
It improves on No Skill in 16 of the 22
families and uses 21% fewer acquisition tokens than
Post-hoc Teaching.
The 95% bootstrap confidence interval over task families for Fixed-Window SSL–Trace2Skill is
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1.45,6.49]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1.45</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6.49</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1.45,6.49]</annotation></semantics></math> percentage points. The intervals for Post-hoc Teaching–Expert Authoring,
Fixed-Window SSL–Post-hoc Teaching, and Fixed-Window SSL–Expert Authoring are respectively
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1.57,5.64]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.57</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5.64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1.57,5.64]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2.34,9.09]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2.34</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9.09</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2.34,9.09]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[3.62,11.44]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>3.62</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11.44</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[3.62,11.44]</annotation></semantics></math> points.
The Fixed-Window SSL–adapted SKILL-KD interval is
<math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1.79,8.48]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1.79</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8.48</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1.79,8.48]</annotation></semantics></math> points. All intervals resample the same paired family
differences.</p>
</div>
