<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Additional model pairs</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 / DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813 and Kimi K2.5 / Kimi K3
independently acquire packages on a
10-family, 77-case lite subset of the main
cohort: Audio STFT peaks (10 cases), Filter JS from HTML (10), Git leak recovery (6), HTML finance verification (6), JQ processing (7), KV-store gRPC (6), PyPI server (10), SPARQL professors (10), SQLite truncation (6), and XLSX structure (6). Each condition has 1 repeat, 3
acquisition rounds, and 77 held-out evaluations in fresh
sessions with equal weighting across task families. Each model-pair
experiment comprises 40 acquisition runs,
120 anchor evaluations by fresh solvers,
308 Skill-based held-out evaluations, and
77 No-Skill evaluations, and compares four
acquisition protocols and No Skill.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On all three model pairs, the two interleaved protocols take the top two
positions and Expert Authoring ranks third (Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 RQ2: Organizing expert guidance during Skill acquisition ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>(a)).
Fixed-Window SSL exceeds Post-hoc Teaching by 4.88,
2.54, and 4.09 points on the shared
families for Qwen, DeepSeek, and Kimi, respectively.
Fixed-Window SSL has the highest mean utility in both additional pairs, gaining
3.08 and 8.24 points over the respective No-Skill
solvers; Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ D.3 Additional model pairs ‣ Appendix D Supplementary Transfer Results ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> gives the complete comparison.
Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.3 Additional model pairs ‣ Appendix D Supplementary Transfer Results ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> reports paired family bootstrap intervals for
the headline contrasts, and Table <a href="#A4.T14" title="Table 14 ‣ D.3 Additional model pairs ‣ Appendix D Supplementary Transfer Results ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> lists the
per-family scores.</p>
</div>
