<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Teaching-intervention taxonomy and dialogue turns</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Educator records intent labels when issuing each teaching tool call.
These labels describe its intended change in learner state.
A lesson may receive multiple labels; silence is a separate decision.
The codebook distinguishes task knowledge, reasoning, evidence acquisition,
diagnosis, calibration, and consolidation, following the emphasis on task,
process, and self-regulation in feedback research and active construction
during tutoring <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hattie and Timperley, 2007</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chi et al., 2001</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
