<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Learning progress and review cost</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each of the 66 runs completes all 3 acquisition rounds,
with practice continuing after anchor success. We link the resulting 198
fresh-solver anchor evaluations to package snapshots. The unit of analysis
is a later round paired with its preceding anchor result, yielding
132 transitions with comparable snapshots.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.17860v1/review_behavior.svg" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/182;" width="476" height="182"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="A5.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Teaching emphasis and development after anchor success.</span>
Qwen Fixed-Window SSL (<math id="A5.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=10</annotation></semantics></math>), 22 families and 66 acquisition runs.
(a) Educator-reported intents in first-round versus later lessons; labels
may overlap. (b) Package revisions in rounds following a perfect anchor
score, grouped by whether a new lesson arrives.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Teaching across rounds.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>a uses regular-review lesson counts of
170/233,
42/112, and
14/87. Including trajectory-end
reviews gives 188/299,
47/178, and 19/153.
Utility on anchor tests by fresh solvers is 0.824, 0.986, and
0.990, with 38/66,
61/66, and 63/66 perfect
results. Figure <a href="#A5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ E.3 Learning progress and review cost ‣ Appendix E Teaching Process Analysis ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>a compares 188 first-round lessons with
66 later lessons; reasoning tags occur in
140 versus 28 and diagnosis tags
in 62 versus 37.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Development after anchor success.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Of the 132 later-round transitions, 99
follow a perfect anchor (38 second rounds and
61 third rounds), covering 61 runs and all
22 families. Packages change in 98/
99: 32/33
rounds with a new lesson and 66/66
without one. Those 33 rounds contain
35 lessons. Across all later rounds, the
76 rounds without a new lesson all revise their package. Prior lessons and anchor feedback remain
available.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Review cost before follow-up.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Silent reviews account for 59.7% of review
opportunities and 72.1% of opening-review tokens.
Figure <a href="#S5.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>c includes cached input and excludes follow-up
dialogue. Each round’s teaching and silent token totals are divided by its
total review count, so stacked heights give mean cost per review.
Round totals are 22.3M, 49.9M, and
60.5M tokens; silent shares are 40.4%,
69.8%, and 85.8%.
Average token use per review rises from 74.7K to
395.7K tokens per review across acquisition rounds, a
5.3-fold increase. Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Review Scheduling and Cost Allocation ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> reports
schedule-level costs including follow-up dialogue.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The corresponding teaching sessions and training-iteration evaluations are
released under <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">experiments/main/qwen/fixed-window-ssl/</span>; each run’s <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">meta.json</span> lists
its session inventory.</p>
</div>
</section>
