<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fixed-Window SSL uses 158.2M Educator tokens across 630
reviews; Issue-Guided SSL uses 60.6M across
329. The 47.8% reduction in reviews combines
with a 26.7% reduction in tokens per review
(251.1K to 184.1K), yielding a
61.7% reduction in Educator tokens.
These per-review costs include follow-up dialogue. Issue-Guided SSL combines
issue-triggered review with local context and its follow-up policy; the
protocol settings are detailed in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Acquisition loop and review events ‣ Appendix C Protocols, Implementation, and Reproduction ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ F.1 Schedules and role-level cost ‣ Appendix F Review Scheduling and Cost Allocation ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> puts reductions in Educator tokens and
changed learner work on the same scale, in millions of tokens per run.
Positive net savings mean fewer acquisition tokens within the recorded scope.
Student tokens fall 16.1% on Kimi but rise
39.2% on DeepSeek, where the additional Student work
exceeds the Educator saving. These outcomes distinguish the consistent
reduction in external supervision from the model-dependent change in
total acquisition cost.</p>
</div>
