<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Case Evidence and Frozen-Package Use</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Testing and adapting Educator guidance</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The HTML-finance case comes from Qwen <span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Fixed-Window SSL</span>, repeat 1, in the
main 22-family cohort. It follows a teaching proposal through
Student execution, package revision, and fresh use
(Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 RQ3: How teaching enters Skill development ‣ 5 Can SSL Develop Transferable Agent Skills? ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">From a proposal to a checked procedure.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Educator recommends deriving reported financial values from other entries
and distinguishing agreement, disagreement, and the absence of an applicable
rule. It also suggests generic arithmetic search. The Student implements
and runs this strategy on the anchor. The resulting verifier flags
4 metrics and selects line 140, although the incorrect
entry is the gross margin at line 210.
Inspecting the output, the Student identifies missing financial derivations
and replaces generic arithmetic with relations appropriate to each metric,
including reverse derivations. Running the revised verifier on the same
report leaves only line 210 flagged: the reported gross margin
is 60.8%, while <math id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="520.4/842.0\times 100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>520.4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>842.0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">520.4/842.0\times 100</annotation></semantics></math> rounds to 61.8%.
The contrast records two executions during acquisition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Retained knowledge and fresh use.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The final <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SKILL.md</span> retains three outcomes—confirmed, contradicted,
and unchecked—and instructs solvers to use both forward and reverse
financial relations. It bundles the revised <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">verify.py</span>.
On held-out <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">v14</span>, a fresh solver reads both resources and checks
relations in a cash-flow statement. Operating, investing, and financing
subtotals sum to 8,000, whereas the reported net increase is 6,270.
The closing cash balance independently agrees with 8,000. The solver submits
<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">4206,6270</span>, identifying the erroneous line and its reported value,
and passes 4/4 checks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Source records.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The released run is <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">experiments/main/qwen/fixed-window-ssl/r1/html-finance-verify/</span>.
Within it, <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">skill-formation/student-author.jsonl</span> contains the lesson
and two executions (records 20 and 42–44); <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">heldout/v14.jsonl</span>
contains package reads, accounting checks, and submission (records 4, 10,
12, and 14). Scores for all six held-out cases are in <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">meta.json</span>.
Record numbers refer to the JSONL <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">i</span> field.</p>
</div>
