<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Flask issue reopening: event-level evidence</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a Qwen Issue-Guided SSL Flask run, <span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">issue-1</span> receives a
lesson, revision, and no-lesson closure during the first round. Fresh-solver anchor
feedback with 6/9 checks and missing-table errors reopens it in the next round. The renewed
lesson identifies an import-bound database path: a changed working directory
can redirect the service to the wrong database. The Student reproduces
the mismatch, resolves paths at request time, and reports 14/14 local
checks before verification-backed closure. Separately,
fresh-solver anchor utility is 0.667, 1.000, and
1.000 across rounds.
The released run is <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">experiments/main/qwen/issue-guided-ssl/r3/flask/</span>.
Its session logs are restored with the command in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Protocols, Implementation, and Reproduction ‣ Socratic Skill Learning: Interleaving Teaching and Practice for Transferable Agent Skills" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.
In <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_path ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">skill-formation/student-author.jsonl</span>, records 50 and 52 show
the anchor feedback and renewed guidance; records 80–82 show verification
and the revision addressing the issue.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Limitations</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our study evaluates complete Skill-learning protocols under a shared
single-anchor setting. Further controlled comparisons could isolate how
much the Educator, review timing, and issue structure each contribute to
transfer performance and teaching cost.</p>
</div>
